# grammar: v0 (unfrozen; AST normative)
#
# The saltmarket world — the shared test corpus every later lane checks against.
# Gentle subset plus a chronology spine: an era spine (>=3 eras), events with a
# before-fact and a deliberately UNORDERED pair, states with since/until (the
# two-era water-status case), an adjacency graph (>=6 edges), and a question with
# options under a hypothesis. Provenance is this world's OWN decision list
# (d-0001..d-0009) — a solo writer's ledger, per 01-syntax §3.
scope saltmarket

# --- world chronology: a totally-ordered era spine (>=3 eras) -----------------
era first-tides < the-silting < the-drought-years < the-ledger-days   decided d-0001

# events carry era membership; WITHIN an era only `before` orders them
event the-first-weir       during first-tides        decided d-0002
event the-silting-begins   during the-silting        decided d-0002
event the-long-drought     during the-drought-years  decided d-0003
event the-marsh-enclosure  during the-drought-years  decided d-0003
event the-salt-tithe       during the-drought-years  proposed
event the-ledger-struck    during the-ledger-days    decided d-0009

# a declared intra-era order:
before the-long-drought -> the-marsh-enclosure       decided d-0003
# ...and a DELIBERATELY UNORDERED pair: the-salt-tithe shares the-drought-years
# with the-long-drought but no before-fact orders them, so
# happens-before(the-salt-tithe, the-long-drought) answers `unordered` — a
# first-class verdict, not a silent tie-break (03-time §1).

narration vantage the-ledger-days
# inert: the narrator looks back from the ledger-days; declaring an event here
# is a type error (03-time §1.iii)

# --- places and the adjacency graph (7 places, >=6 edges) ---------------------
place saltmarket    "Saltmarket"      decided d-0004
place the-shallows  "The Shallows"    decided d-0004
place the-weir      "The Weir"        decided d-0004
place the-tideflats "The Tideflats"   decided d-0005
place the-cut       "The Cut"         decided d-0005
place the-old-quay  "The Old Quay"    decided d-0005
place the-fen-road  "The Fen Road"    proposed

adjacent(saltmarket, the-shallows)     decided d-0004
adjacent(the-shallows, the-weir)       decided d-0004
adjacent(the-weir, the-tideflats)      decided d-0005
adjacent(saltmarket, the-cut)          decided d-0005
adjacent(the-cut, the-old-quay)        decided d-0005
adjacent(the-old-quay, the-fen-road)   proposed
adjacent(the-fen-road, the-tideflats)  proposed

# --- people, a thing, and facts -----------------------------------------------
person mara     "Mara of the Weirs"    decided d-0006
person old-fen  "Old Fen"              decided d-0006
thing the-salt-ledger "The Salt-Ledger" decided d-0007

fact mara lives-in saltmarket          decided d-0006
fact old-fen tends the-weir            decided d-0006

# --- states: facts acquire validity spans (the two-era water-status case) ----
state the-weir.water = common   until the-marsh-enclosure   decided d-0008
state the-weir.water = enclosed since the-marsh-enclosure   decided d-0008
# common UNTIL the enclosure and enclosed SINCE it: a pre-enclosure flashback
# checks clean AND the present checks clean, because the two claims hold over
# disjoint spans (03-time §2). No false contradiction between them.

# --- an open fork: a question with options under a hypothesis ------------------
hypothesis h-ledger "the salt-ledger was kept by the marsh-folk, not the guild"

question who-keeps-the-ledger "Who keeps the salt-ledger?"
  option old-fen  implies keeps(old-fen, the-salt-ledger)
  option mara     implies keeps(mara, the-salt-ledger)   assumes h-ledger
# proposed-first: neither option is canon until a ruling; the question is a
# tracked debt, not a blank (01-syntax §4).
